---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import { breadcrumbs } from '../../components/_breadcrumbs';
import { downloads } from '../../config/downloads';

const crumbs = breadcrumbs([{ name: 'Compare', href: '/compare/' }, { name: 'Niyora vs Apple Cycle Tracking', href: '/compare/niyora-vs-apple-cycle-tracking/' }]);
---

<Page
  title="Niyora vs Apple Cycle Tracking: past the prediction · Niyora"
  description="Apple Health logs your period and predicts your window, then stops. Niyora predicts your PMS window too, then helps you through the days it points to."
  canonicalUrl="https://niyora.com/compare/niyora-vs-apple-cycle-tracking/"
  jsonLd={crumbs}
>
  <section class="s hero">
    <div class="eyebrow">Niyora vs Apple Cycle Tracking</div>
    <h1>Apple logs your cycle. Niyora helps you through the hard hour.</h1>
    <p class="lead">Apple Health's Cycle Tracking is built-in logging. You record your period and symptoms, it predicts your next window, and there it stops. Niyora tracks and predicts your PMS window too, but it does not stop at the prediction. When a premenstrual feeling actually lands, it helps you reflect, regulate, and respond in about a minute, and its training builds the skill before you need it.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="s">
    <div class="moat">
      <p>Built-in logging tells you it is coming, then leaves you to handle it. Niyora predicts the same window, then <strong>shows up when it lands</strong>: reflect, regulate, respond in about a minute, and training that builds the skill before you need it. The prediction is where built-in logging finishes. For Niyora it is where the help starts.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="s">
    <h2>The difference, line by line</h2>
    <div class="compare-grid">
      <div class="compare-head them">Built-in logging like Apple Cycle Tracking</div>
      <div class="compare-head us">Niyora</div>

      <div class="compare-cell them"><p>Records your period and predicts your next window. Once it predicts, its job is done.</p></div>
      <div class="compare-cell us"><p>Tracks and predicts your window too, then walks you through reflect, regulate, respond when it lands.</p></div>

      <div class="compare-cell them"><p>You enter the data, and the prediction is the finish line.</p></div>
      <div class="compare-cell us"><p>Training builds the skill before the window, so it lands lighter when it comes.</p></div>

      <div class="compare-cell them"><p>Emotional support is not the point. It is a health record and a prediction.</p></div>
      <div class="compare-cell us"><p>A way to see the moment differently, settle your body, and respond without regret.</p></div>

      <div class="compare-cell them"><p>Success is an accurate record and a reliable prediction.</p></div>
      <div class="compare-cell us"><p>Success is you moving through the moment, and needing it less.</p></div>

      <div class="compare-cell them"><p>Covers the whole cycle as part of a general health app.</p></div>
      <div class="compare-cell us"><p>Built for one window only. The days before your period, when feelings run high.</p></div>

      <div class="compare-cell them"><p>Your data lives in your health record so it can predict across cycles.</p></div>
      <div class="compare-cell us"><p>No account, no sign in. Your personal details are stripped before anything reaches the AI.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="s">
    <div class="honest">
      <h2>To be fair to Apple Cycle Tracking</h2>
      <p>It is already on your phone, it is private to your device, and a reliable prediction is real value. Niyora tracks and predicts too, so this is not tracker versus no tracker. The difference is what happens after the prediction: Apple gives you the date, Niyora helps you through the days it points to. Apple is a fine place to get the prediction, and many people will want both.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="s">
    <h2>Not sure the hard week is even PMS?</h2>
    <p class="lead">Take the two-minute check and see how your premenstrual week actually hits.</p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a href="/quiz" class="btn">Take the quiz</a>
      <a href={downloads.appStore} class="btn ghost">Get Niyora</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>

<style>
  /* Page-specific only: the moat callout, the line-by-line grid, and the
     to-be-fair block. Shared chrome (sheet, sections, dividers, type scale,
     buttons, footer) comes from Page's global CSS. */
  .moat {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 32px 30px;
    border-radius: 20px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(var(--accent-rgb), 0.28);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
  }
  .moat p { font-size: 21px; font-weight: 300; line-height: 1.5; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.86); max-width: none; margin: 0; }
  .moat strong { color: rgba(var(--accent-rgb), 0.98); font-weight: 500; }

  .compare-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 14px;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 24px auto 0;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .compare-head { font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: 3px; text-transform: uppercase; padding-bottom: 4px; }
  .compare-head.them { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.4); }
  .compare-head.us { color: rgba(var(--accent-rgb), 0.9); }
  .compare-cell {
    padding: 18px 20px;
    border-radius: 14px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
  }
  .compare-cell p { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.55; margin: 0; max-width: none; }
  .compare-cell.them { background: rgba(20, 18, 26, 0.4); }
  .compare-cell.them p { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.52); }
  .compare-cell.us { border-color: rgba(var(--accent-rgb), 0.32); }
  .compare-cell.us p { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.86); }

  .honest { max-width: 680px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .honest p { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.72); font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.6; max-width: none; }

  .cta-row { display: flex; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; margin-top: 28px; }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .s { padding: 56px 24px; }
    h1 { font-size: 34px; }
    h2 { font-size: 26px; }
    .moat p { font-size: 18px; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .compare-grid { gap: 10px 12px; }
    .compare-cell { padding: 14px 16px; }
  }
</style>
